---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Subscriptions and Refunds Policy - Banners All Over" description="Subscriptions and Refunds Policy for Banners All Over Shopify app subscriptions">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} class="nav-link inline-flex items-center text-bao-blue hover:text-bao-blue-600 transition-colors mb-6">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Subscriptions and Refunds Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600">Last Updated: December 9, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="legal-content prose prose-lg max-w-none">

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Introduction</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          This Subscriptions and Refunds Policy explains how subscriptions to Banners All Over ("we," "us," "our," or "BAO") work, how you can cancel your subscription, and under what circumstances refunds are provided.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          All subscriptions to Banners All Over are processed through Shopify's billing system. By subscribing to a paid plan, you agree to the terms outlined in this policy as well as Shopify's billing terms.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Please read this policy carefully before subscribing to any of our paid plans.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Subscription Plans -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. Subscription Plans and Billing</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.1 Available Plans</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Banners All Over offers four subscription tiers: Basic (Free), Standard, Pro, and Business. Each tier includes different features, banner limits, and pricing options.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          For current pricing details, including monthly and annual billing options, please visit our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}#pricing`} class="text-bao-blue hover:underline font-semibold">Pricing page</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.2 Billing Cycles</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Monthly Subscriptions:</strong> Billed on the same day each month from when you subscribed</li>
          <li><strong>Annual Subscriptions:</strong> Billed once per year on the anniversary of your subscription date</li>
          <li><strong>Free Plan:</strong> No billing; available indefinitely with limited features</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.3 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          All payments are processed by Shopify through their app billing system. We do not directly handle or store your payment information.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          For questions about payment processing, please refer to <a href="https://www.shopify.com/legal/terms-payments-us" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shopify's Payment Terms</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.4 Automatic Renewal</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Your subscription will automatically renew at the end of each billing period unless you cancel before the renewal date by downgrading to the Free Plan or uninstalling the app (see Section 3). You will be charged the then-current price for your subscription plan.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700">
          <strong>Renewal Notifications:</strong> We may send you a reminder before your subscription renews, but you are responsible for tracking your renewal date and taking action (downgrading or uninstalling) if you no longer wish to continue with a paid plan.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Cancellation Policy -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">3. Cancellation Policy</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.1 Canceling Your Paid Plan (Downgrade to Free)</h3>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If you want to stop being charged but continue using Banners All Over with basic features, downgrading to the <strong>Free Basic Plan</strong> is the recommended option. This allows you to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Stop all charges:</strong> The Free Plan is free forever—no billing required</li>
          <li><strong>Keep using the app:</strong> Continue with limited banners and slides (see our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}#pricing`} class="text-bao-blue hover:underline">Pricing section</a> for exact limits)</li>
          <li><strong>Preserve your data:</strong> All your banners and settings are retained (excess banners are disabled but not deleted)</li>
          <li><strong>Re-upgrade anytime:</strong> Easily return to a paid plan whenever you need more features</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.1.1 How to Downgrade</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          To downgrade to the Free Basic Plan:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>Open the <strong>Banners All Over</strong> app in your Shopify admin</li>
          <li>Go to <strong>Settings</strong> or <strong>Account</strong></li>
          <li>Click <strong>Change Plan</strong> or <strong>Manage Subscription</strong></li>
          <li>Select <strong>Free Basic Plan</strong></li>
          <li>Confirm your downgrade</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>When does it take effect?</strong> Your downgrade takes effect at the <strong>end of your current billing period</strong>. Until then, you continue to have full access to your current plan's features.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>When do charges stop?</strong> You will be charged the current plan price for the remainder of this billing period, then <strong>no charges</strong> starting from your next billing cycle (since the Free Plan is free).
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Important:</strong> Downgrading is not refundable for the current billing period; you will only be charged the new lower price (free) starting from your next billing cycle.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.1.2 What Happens to Your Data</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you downgrade to the Free Basic Plan:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>All Data Retained:</strong> Your banner data, settings, and media files are never deleted</li>
          <li><strong>Free Plan Limits:</strong> The Free Plan allows fewer banners and slides than paid plans (see our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}#pricing`} class="text-bao-blue hover:underline">Pricing section</a> for exact limits)</li>
          <li><strong>Excess Banners Disabled:</strong> Banners or slides exceeding the Free Plan limits will be <strong>disabled but not deleted</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Easy Recovery:</strong> Your excess banners remain in your account and will be automatically re-enabled if you upgrade back to a higher plan</li>
          <li><strong>Visible in Dashboard:</strong> Disabled banners will appear in your dashboard marked as "Disabled - requires Standard Plan or higher"</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>For Paid Plan Subscribers:</strong> When downgrading between plans or to the Free Plan, any banners exceeding your new plan's limit will be disabled but retained. For exact banner and slide limits for each plan, please refer to our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}#pricing`} class="text-bao-blue hover:underline">Pricing section</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-8">3.2 Completely Removing the App (Uninstallation)</h3>

        <div class="bg-red-50 p-4 mb-4 rounded border border-red-200">
          <p class="text-gray-700">
            <strong>Warning:</strong> Only choose this option if you want to completely terminate your use of Banners All Over. Consider downgrading to the Free Plan instead (see Section 3.1).
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If you've decided to completely remove Banners All Over from your Shopify store, you can uninstall the app through your Shopify admin:
        </p>

        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>Log in to your Shopify admin panel</li>
          <li>Go to <strong>Apps</strong> in the left sidebar</li>
          <li>Find <strong>Banners All Over</strong> in your installed apps</li>
          <li>Click the <strong>Delete</strong> or <strong>Uninstall</strong> button</li>
          <li>Confirm the uninstallation</li>
        </ol>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">What Happens When You Uninstall</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you uninstall the Banners All Over app:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Immediate Effect:</strong> Your subscription is canceled immediately upon uninstallation</li>
          <li><strong>No Further Charges:</strong> You will not be charged for any future billing cycles</li>
          <li><strong>Loss of Access:</strong> You will lose access to the app and all its features immediately</li>
          <li><strong>Data Retention:</strong> Your data is retained for 30 days in case you reinstall (see Section 7 for details)</li>
          <li><strong>Permanent Deletion:</strong> After 30 days, all your banner data, settings, and media files are permanently deleted and cannot be recovered</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-red-50 p-4 mb-4 rounded border border-red-200">
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          <strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> Unlike some subscription services, uninstalling the app means you lose access immediately, regardless of whether you've paid for the current billing period.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          If you want to continue using the app until the end of your paid period, keep the app installed until that date, or downgrade to the Free Plan instead.
        </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Need assistance?</strong> If you need help canceling or have questions about your options, please <a href="#questions-support" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline font-semibold">contact our support team</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-8">3.3 Comparison: Downgrade vs. Uninstall</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Not sure whether to downgrade or completely uninstall? Here's a quick comparison to help you decide:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
          <table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg">
            <thead class="bg-gray-100">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b">Aspect</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b">Downgrade to Free</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b">Complete Uninstall</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">When effective?</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">End of current billing period</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Immediately</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b bg-gray-50">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Charges stop when?</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">End of current period</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Immediately</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Your banners</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Disabled but kept (can re-enable if upgrade)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Permanently deleted after 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b bg-gray-50">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Slides and media</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Disabled but kept</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Permanently deleted after 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Can you use the app?</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Yes, with limited banners and slides (see Pricing)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">No access to app</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b bg-gray-50">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Data recovery window</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">N/A (always preserved)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">30 days (reinstall to recover)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Can you change your mind?</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Yes, upgrade anytime</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Yes, reinstall within 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">Recommended for...</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Testing features, cost savings, seasonal use</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">No longer need banners at all</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 mb-4 rounded">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Decision Helper</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-2"><strong>Choose downgrade if you:</strong></p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Want to save money but might need banners again in the future</li>
            <li>Only need limited features (Free Plan has fewer banners/slides than paid plans)</li>
            <li>Might upgrade during peak seasons or promotional periods</li>
            <li>Want to keep your banner designs and settings for later use</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-2"><strong>Choose uninstall if you:</strong></p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1">
            <li>Definitely don't need banners in the foreseeable future</li>
            <li>Want to completely remove the app from your Shopify admin</li>
            <li>Have already saved all content you need</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Our Recommendation:</strong> We recommend downgrading to the Free Plan unless you're certain you'll never use the app again. This preserves your work and gives you flexibility for the future.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-8">3.4 Changing Your Plan or Getting Help</h3>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">Re-Upgrading from Free Plan</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          You can upgrade from the Free Plan to any paid plan at any time:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>How to Upgrade:</strong> Open the app, go to Settings or Account, and select your desired paid plan</li>
          <li><strong>Billing:</strong> Your new billing period starts immediately upon upgrade</li>
          <li><strong>Data Restoration:</strong> Your previously disabled banners and slides become accessible again automatically when you upgrade to the same plan you had before</li>
          <li><strong>No Data Loss:</strong> Your banners, settings, and media are preserved exactly as you left them</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">Reinstalling After Uninstall</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If you uninstalled the app but changed your mind:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Within 30 Days:</strong> Reinstall the app from the Shopify App Store, and your data will be automatically restored</li>
          <li><strong>After 30 Days:</strong> Your data has been permanently deleted. You can still reinstall, but you'll start fresh with a new account</li>
          <li><strong>Billing:</strong> Reinstalling starts a new subscription and billing period</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">Need Help Deciding?</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If you're unsure whether to downgrade, uninstall, or which plan is right for you, please <a href="#questions-support" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline font-semibold">contact our support team</a>. We're happy to discuss options for continuing to use Banners All Over or help you make the best decision for your needs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Refund Policy -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">4. Refund Policy</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.1 General Refund Policy</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Monthly Subscriptions:</strong> Generally non-refundable. When you cancel, you receive access through the end of your paid period, which serves as your "money's worth."
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Annual Subscriptions:</strong> Generally non-refundable. When you cancel, you retain access through the end of your paid annual period, which serves as your "money's worth." However, refunds may be granted at our discretion in special circumstances outlined in Section 4.2 below.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.2 Exceptions and Special Circumstances</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We may provide refunds at our sole discretion in the following circumstances:
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Technical Issues:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>If the app experiences a <strong>major outage or malfunction</strong> that prevents core functionality for an extended period (e.g., 7+ consecutive days)</li>
          <li>If we <strong>discontinue the service</strong> before the end of your paid period, you will receive a pro-rated refund for the unused portion</li>
          <li>If there is a <strong>billing error</strong> where you were charged incorrectly or multiple times</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Service Not as Described:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>If the app <strong>fundamentally fails to deliver</strong> the features described on our pricing page and documentation</li>
          <li>Refund requests based on this reason must be submitted within <strong>7 days of subscription</strong></li>
          <li>You must provide specific details about which features are not functioning as described</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Incompatibility Issues:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>If our app is <strong>incompatible with your Shopify theme</strong> and we are unable to resolve the issue within 14 days</li>
          <li>Must be reported within <strong>14 days of subscription</strong></li>
          <li>Requires cooperation with our support team to attempt resolution</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.3 Non-Refundable Circumstances</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Refunds will <strong>NOT</strong> be provided in the following situations:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Change of mind:</strong> You simply no longer want to use the app</li>
          <li><strong>Failure to use:</strong> You subscribed but never used the app or features</li>
          <li><strong>Duplicate purchases:</strong> You subscribed to multiple plans by mistake (but we can help you cancel duplicates)</li>
          <li><strong>Violation of Terms:</strong> Your account was terminated for violating our Terms of Service</li>
          <li><strong>User error:</strong> Misunderstanding of features, failure to configure properly, or not reading documentation</li>
          <li><strong>Dissatisfied with the results:</strong> The app didn't improve your sales or conversions as you expected.</li>
          <li><strong>Forgot to cancel:</strong> You forgot to cancel before auto-renewal (but we can help you cancel going forward)</li>
          <li><strong>Minor bugs or issues:</strong> Small bugs that don't prevent core functionality and are being addressed</li>
          <li><strong>Price changes:</strong> Requesting a refund or price adjustment due to recent changes in subscription pricing</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.4 How to Request a Refund</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          To request a refund, please follow these steps:
        </p>

        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-3">
          <li>
            <strong>Contact Support:</strong> <a href="#questions-support" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline font-semibold">See section 8</a> for contact details
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1">
              <li>Subject line: "Refund Request"</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Provide Required Information:</strong>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1">
              <li>Your Shopify store URL</li>
              <li>Email address associated with your account</li>
              <li>Subscription plan and billing cycle (monthly/annual)</li>
              <li>Date of purchase</li>
              <li>Detailed reason for refund request</li>
              <li>Any relevant screenshots or documentation</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Allow Time for Review:</strong> We will review your request within <strong>5 business days</strong> and respond via email
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Refund Processing:</strong> If approved, refunds are processed through Shopify and typically appear within <strong>5-10 business days</strong> depending on your payment method
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.5 Refund Timeframe</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Request Review:</strong> 5 business days to review and approve/deny</li>
          <li><strong>Processing:</strong> 3-5 business days after approval</li>
          <li><strong>Bank/Card Processing:</strong> Additional 5-10 business days depending on your financial institution</li>
          <li><strong>Total Time:</strong> Up to 20 business days from request to funds in your account</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Free Trial -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">5. Free Trials (If Applicable)</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          [SPECIFY IF YOU OFFER FREE TRIALS]
        </p>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2">
            <strong>If free trials are offered:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>Trial duration: [e.g., 7 days, 14 days, 30 days]</li>
            <li>Access: Full access to [specify plan level] features during trial</li>
            <li>Billing: No charges during trial period</li>
            <li>Cancellation: Cancel anytime during trial without being charged</li>
            <li>Auto-Conversion: If not canceled, trial automatically converts to paid subscription at the end of the trial period</li>
            <li>Reminder: Email notification [X days] before trial ends</li>
            <li>One Per Customer: Free trials are limited to one per Shopify store</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Price Changes -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">6. Price Changes</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We reserve the right to modify our pricing at any time. Price changes will be handled as follows:
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">6.1 Notice Period</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Existing Subscribers:</strong> At least 30 days' advance notice via email before any price increase</li>
          <li><strong>New Subscribers:</strong> New prices apply immediately upon subscription</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">6.2 When Price Changes Take Effect</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Monthly Subscriptions:</strong> New price applies at your next billing cycle after the notice period</li>
          <li><strong>Annual Subscriptions:</strong> New price applies at your next annual renewal date</li>
          <li><strong>Grandfathering:</strong> We may grandfather existing customers at their current price for a limited time at our discretion</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">6.3 Your Options</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          If you do not agree to a price increase, you may downgrade your subscription before the new price takes effect. Your continued use of the service after the price increase date constitutes acceptance of the new pricing.
        </p>
      </section>

